# Panoptes Lens

Flutter app root: `panoptes_lens/`. Read `AGENTS.md` at repo root for full briefing.

## One codebase, one truth

- There is **one** implementation per screen. Never create parallel versions (`*_v2`, `*_pdf`, `*_designer`).
- **Working behavior beats mockup fidelity.** The app already ran end-to-end before styling work.
- Do not merge or rewrite large swaths to "match the PDF." Skin incrementally via `lib/theme/tokens.dart`.

## Design PDF is style-only

`Panoptes_Lens___Design_System.pdf` (Claude Designer output) is a **visual reference** — palette, typography, layout mood, copy tone.

It is **not** a spec to reimplement line-by-line. Prior sessions treated it as gospel, rewrote working code, and broke the pipeline in a merge/rewrite loop.

When styling: preserve Riverpod providers, navigation, and pipeline hooks. Change appearance, not architecture.

## Sacred — ask before changing

- `panoptes_lens/lib/api/prompts.dart` — the product; never expose in UI; do not shorten
- `panoptes_lens/lib/api/pipeline.dart` — stage orchestration
- `panoptes_lens/lib/api/claude_client.dart` — streaming + errors
- `panoptes_lens/lib/models/analysis.dart` — lenient parsers

## Resolved decisions (do not re-open)

- State: **Riverpod** (`inputProvider`, `pipelineRunProvider`, `analysisProvider`)
- Voice: **speech_to_text**
- Models: see `lib/config/api_config.dart` (not stale `handoff.md`)

## UI conventions

- All colors/type from `lib/theme/tokens.dart` — no raw `Color()` in widgets
- Empty parsed fields are normal; UI must handle gracefully
- Prompts are never user-visible

## Before finishing UI work

Run `flutter analyze` from `panoptes_lens/`. Do not leave broken imports or duplicate screen implementations.
